        "math_academy_id": "q-275511",
        "problem": "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+2z=5 \\\\ 2x+6y+5z=22 \\\\ x-2y-3z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $1$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $6$ | $5$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | $1$ | $-2$ | {{field-4}} |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-1$ |  |  |",
        "worked_solution": "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+2z=5 \\\\ 2x+6y+5z=22 \\\\ x-2y-3z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 22 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 22 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
